ion","label":"Intuition","html_id":"intuition","implicit":true,"key":"SlHYU7Yu1y"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Book sales are a natural “winner-take-more” setting.  Most titles sell little\nin a given week, while a few sell much more.  A rank is not the same object as\na sales count, but if sales approximately follow a power law, a log-log plot of\nsales against rank can look close to linear over part of the range.","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"UdW44EXGco"}],"key":"LzrxddDoda"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The important word is “approximately.”  Amazon’s ranking algorithm is not a\nstatistical law of nature, and this old dataset is small.  The example is a\nreal-data bridge from the Pareto pages to rank-size empirical work.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"p111xHljM5"}],"key":"Qjdvu7ugdV"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Proof","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"yRW5zIB9hN"}],"identifier":"proof","label":"Proof","html_id":"proof","implicit":true,"key":"WnyWIDw8HX"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There is no proof that the data are Pareto.  The computation is a reproducible\ndiagnostic:","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"sfkNVgVPPj"}],"key":"EtnzILQqib"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"